  "configuration_id": "config_037",
  "reason": "The current best configuration (config_031: scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool, weighted fusion, ResNet50) achieves 0.678 accuracy, but the image channel's contribution is uncertain because ResNet50 was very weak in isolation (0.208 accuracy image-only). The key question is whether the image modality's ~2.8-point gain over RNA-only is encoder-limited (i.e., a stronger encoder like ViT-L could unlock more complementary signal) or fundamentally limited by the image data's discriminative content. Config_037 changes only the image encoder from ResNet50 to imagenet_vit_l while holding all other settings (scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool, weighted fusion) constant, providing a clean single-variable comparison against config_031. This is the highest-information next experiment: if ViT-L substantially improves accuracy, it confirms the image channel has untapped potential and justifies further multimodal investment; if it does not, it indicates the image contribution is near its ceiling and the current configuration is close to optimal. This is preferred over testing transformer aggregation (config_033), which is low-value given the near-identical RNA-only results (0.653 vs 0.650), and over changing multiple variables simultaneously."
}

